From 1727818b77b9b017385c79073d8e1e6b9a60472b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikhil Prakash <nikhil.prakash1995@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:11:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Test register: per-option, harness/stats, Python, Phase 2
 and promote-step test bodies (TSR Phase 3, WM-2 A7)

build_register.py gains a static source parser: every it() under
test/L2-identity-system/per-option and test/benchmarks, and every test
function under 2_w3c-ssi-layer, cv2x-testbed/tests, sandbox/py-suites,
phase2 and tools/run_identity, gets a TC entry; subject, function and
class come from docs/testing/unit_rules.yaml and each entry records the
rule that mapped it. No test title is edited. The 305 results-derived
entries are unchanged; 675 entries added (639 tests in the four main
bodies; Python count equals pytest's 333 distinct collected functions).
--check-complete fails on a tracked test file that is neither registered,
results-derived nor excluded with a reason, and on a parse/token count
mismatch; both probes shown to fail. The coverage page gains a generated
subject x class table for these bodies.
